.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Agent/harness state. Excluded because session transcripts have been observed
# to contain a live Bright Data API token. Never commit this directory.
.claude/

# --- dependencies ------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# Vendored third-party bundle, reproducible with `npm run vendor`.
# Kept out of history so the repo stays readable.
app/vendor/

# --- corpus ------------------------------------------------------------------
# corpus/ IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
# 77 archived HTML captures of three public product-recall pages, Jan 2024 to
# Aug 2026, fetched from the Internet Archive. 14 MB raw, ~2 MB packed.
#
# Every number this project publishes is a measurement over these files. Without
# them `npm test` and `npm run bench` cannot run on a fresh clone and none of the
# results are verifiable, which for a project whose entire claim is a measurement
# is worse than the disk cost. manifest.json records each capture's URL,
# timestamp and content digest so `npm run corpus` reproduces it exactly.

# --- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
# results/ IS COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
# The hackathon requires "example structured output" as a submission artifact,
# and these files are the evidence behind every claim in the README:
#   events.jsonl      74 proof records, one per run, heals and abstentions alike
#   bench.json        the benchmark, 135 cases with exact ground truth
#   sweep.json        110 threshold pairs, the calibration behind tau and delta
#   ikea-recalls.json 60 live records from Bright Data collector c_mt1nrjboski90goqc
# Excluding them would make the numbers unverifiable and the submission
# non-qualifying.
#
# The raw .ndjson is Bright Data's unmodified API response. It is the most
# authentic example output in the repo and tools/audit.js reads it by default,
# so it is committed too.

# --- os / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- derived --------------------------------------------------------------
# Content-addressed page captures. Regenerable with `npm run replay`, so they
# are evidence you can rebuild rather than evidence you must keep.
captures/
